# Backend laws

## Packages

- `backend/auth` — session cookies, Selenium, prolongation only.
- `backend/kontur` — Kontur HTTP, CryptoPro, WinHTTP.
- `backend/services` — history, aggregation, BarTender labels, queue helpers.
- `backend/app` — ApiBridge (UI contract), desktop entry, optional CHZ bridge.

Do not put UI markup in backend. Do not import `frontend`.

## Contracts

- `ApiBridge` public methods are the stable contract for the React UI. Rename only with a frontend update in the same change.
- Prefer typed dicts / explicit return shapes `{ ok, error, ... }`. Log via project logger, not `print`.
- Session: always validate with live Kontur check when trusting cookies; never TTL-alone.

## Auth / Selenium

- Default: real Yandex profile, off-screen window, Win32 hide. No `--headless=new` unless explicitly opted in.
- Keep XPath automation best-effort with clear logs; failures must not crash the desktop process.

## Files & runtime

- Persist machine-local state under `runtime/` (cookies, logs, CHZ state). Do not commit secrets or live cookie files.
- Label templates live in `assets/labels/`. Resolve paths from repo root helpers, not hard-coded Desktop paths.

## Tests

- Unit-test auth orchestration, ApiBridge session wiring, and pure helpers under `tests/`.
- No network in unit tests — mock Kontur and Selenium.
